# Double drop - both tracks locked and hollowed out, then everything at once.
#
# Sixteen bars of taking things away from both of them: the old one loses its bottom, the
# new one never had any, and by bar twelve there is almost nothing left but midrange on two
# tracks counting the same bars. Then the old one goes and the new one's low end arrives in
# the same instant.
#
# It only works because they are in time with each other, which is what the tempo lane and
# the bar alignment are for. Without a readable tempo the player runs the same moves on a
# timer instead, and it is a good transition rather than a great one.

name    Double drop
note    both hollowed out and locked, then everything lands at once
bars    16
align   beat
power   free

lane out gain
    bar 0     1.0    hold
    bar 11    1.0    smooth
    bar 12    0.0    hold
    bar 16    0.0    hold

lane out bass
    bar 0       0    smooth
    bar 6     -40    hold
    bar 16    -40    hold

lane out lowpass
    bar 8   16000    smooth
    bar 12    500    hold
    bar 16    500    hold

lane in gain
    bar 0     0.0    hold
    bar 4     0.0    smooth
    bar 10    1.0    hold
    bar 16    1.0    hold

lane in bass
    bar 0     -40    hold
    bar 12      0    hold
    bar 16      0    hold

lane in mid
    bar 0     -12    hold
    bar 4     -12    smooth
    bar 10      0    hold
    bar 16      0    hold

# Locked right through the drop, and only released once it is alone.
lane in tempo
    bar 0     0.0    hold
    bar 12    0.0    smooth
    bar 16    1.0    hold

hook bar 10   toast both together
